SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: North Sonoma Mtn ↔ Jack London SHP
DESCRIPTION:The SugarShuttle is heading to North Sonoma Mountain Regional Park and Jack London State Historic Park! Shuttle also offered on Sunday\, May 3 here. \nHow it works: Every half hour our Shuttle will leave from either North Sonoma Mountain Regional Park’s parking lot or Jack London State Historic Park’s upper parking lot or winery lot. Make a reservation and then ride to the other end of the trail\, or hike and ride back. Riding first and hiking back to your car is the easiest way—no worries about how long you take to finish your hike. This 9-mile one-way hike should take 4 to 5 hours\, including nearly 2\,000 feet of elevation gain. If you sign up for the 12:15 pm drop off at N. Sonoma Mtn\, please note that the gate at Jack London SHP closes at 5:00 pm. Bring at least 64oz of water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snack. \nRegistration is required as there is only space for 6 riders at a time\, but you can ride on a space-available basis as well. There is no charge for the ride; the $10 reservation fee is refunded on site the day of the event\, unless you choose to donate it to keep this service running. Dogs and bikes are not allowed in the shuttle or on Jack London’s trails (the State Park portion of the hiking route). Parking fees apply.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/sugarshuttle-north-sonoma-mtn-%e2%86%94-jack-london-shp-4/
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd\, Kenwood\, CA
CATEGORIES:Recreation
GEO:38.4427;-122.533
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Sugarloaf Ridge State Park 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd Kenwood CA;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2605 Adobe Canyon Rd:geo:-122.533,38.4427
END:VEVENT
